window.products.push({"id":525858,"name":"Victorinox Fibrox Pro 12-Inch Straight Edge Butcher Knife","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":46.49,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51frwlg5UTL._AC_SL1200_.jpg","description":"A TRUSTED FAVORITE Slices through the largest cuts of meat with ease, the 12\" Victorinox Fibrox Pro Butcher Knife can handle nearly every butcher task imaginable. Crafted with a comfortable handle, superior weight and balance, and a razor sharp straight edge that rarely requires re-sharpening, this knife is an essential tool for every kitchen. KEY FEATURES High-quality, lightweight European steel. High-quality, lightweight European steel. Handle design reduces hand and wrist fatigue. Handle design reduces hand and wrist fatigue. Fit for butchering whole roasts and large cuts of meat. Fit for butchering whole roasts and large cuts of meat. Straight & hollow ground edge cuts glides through meat. Straight & hollow ground edge cuts glides through meat. Flat spine for extra power and heft. Flat spine for extra power and heft. Built-in finger guard for safety. Built-in finger guard for safety. Non-slip patented Fibrox Pro handle for a secure and comfortable grip no matter the hand size. Non-slip patented Fibrox Pro handle for a secure and comfortable grip no matter the hand size. National Sanitary Foundation (NSF) approved and dishwasher safe. National Sanitary Foundation (NSF) approved and dishwasher safe. CARE AND USE Be good to your knives and they’ll be good to you. Following these simple guidelines will ensure that you get the longest life out of your knife! CLEANING Victorinox Swiss Army recommends washing all knives by hand. For best results, hand wash your knives with a soapy cloth and dry immediately.  While Fibrox Pro knives are dishwasher safe, we recommend hand washing as dishwashers are designed to spray water at a relatively high pressure, which can jostle the silverware and cause the knives to collide, dulling the edge. SHARPENING For optimum performance, knives should be honed after every couple of uses. Proper and frequent use of a honing steel will keep your knives sharper and performing at their best. FORMERLY FORSCHNER In 1937 Victorinox began selling cutlery in America through a Connecticut distributor called R.H. Forschner & Co. A well-known manufacturer of butcher scales, Forschner soon became the exclusive U.S. distributor for Victorinox knives, and was the name by which Victorinox knives were known.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51frwlg5UTL._AC_SL1200_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Victorinox","source_asin":"B078KDXXMV","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-525858","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B078KDXXMV","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B078KDXXMV","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
